Reinvent your world. We are building a modern Wipro. We are an end-to-end digital transformation partner with the boldest ambitions. To realize them, we need people inspired by reinvention. Of yourself, your career, and your skills. We want to see the constant evolution of our business and our industry. It has always been in our DNA - as the world around us changes, so do we. Join a business powered by purpose and a place that empowers you to design your own reinvention.

About Vista Equity Partners&nbsp; 

Vista Equity Partners is a leading global investment firm focused exclusively on enterprise software, data, and technology-enabled businesses. With over $100B in assets under management and a portfolio of 90+ software product companies worldwide, Vista accelerates growth through operational excellence, shared expertise, and long-term partnership. In India, Vista's presence continues to expand with 45+ portfolio companies employing more than 17, 000 professionals across technology, product, customer success, and operations - reinforcing India's strategic role as a hub of innovation and talent within the Vista ecosystem. &nbsp; &nbsp; 

Through its Agentic AI Factory, Vista is embedding Generative AI across its global portfolio - enabling companies to integrate intelligent, responsible AI into products, operations, and decision-making. This initiative is strengthened through portfolio-wide learning programs, leadership workshops, and AI hackathons that foster innovation, build fluency, and accelerate practical AI adoption across teams. &nbsp; 

About Amtech&nbsp; 

Amtech is a leading provider of enterprise software solutions for the packaging, printing, and manufacturing industries. Our integrated systems streamline order management, production planning, scheduling, inventory, and business analytics - empowering customers to drive efficiency, reduce costs, and improve operational performance. With a strong commitment to innovation and customer success, Amtech delivers reliable technology backed by deep industry expertise. &nbsp; 

With Vista's investment and strategic guidance, we combine the agility of a growing technology organization with the scale, stability, and career mobility of a global software ecosystem. &nbsp; 

Our Employee Value Proposition

At Amtech, our people are our greatest differentiator. We create an environment where you can: 

Purpose

Shape the future of manufacturing and supply chain operations by delivering mission-critical enterprise software used by industry-leading organizations. 

Growth

Access continuous learning, leadership development, and cross-portfolio opportunities through Vista's global network - accelerating both technical and managerial career paths. 

Culture

Work in a collaborative, transparent, and people-first environment where values, accountability, and integrity guide every decision. 

Innovation

Engage with cutting-edge technologies, including AI-driven automation, and contribute to modernizing financial systems and operational processes across the business. 

Role Description&nbsp; 

Amtech is seeking a Principal Software Engineer / Architect to serve as the technical authority for our Label Traxx ERP platform and its ecosystem of integrations. This role owns the architecture and long-term technical direction of Label Traxx and the AWS-hosted systems that connect to it - including Cloud API, Batched, Siteline, Data Warehouse, and Supplier integrations - ensuring the platform scales reliably as Amtech's customer base and integration footprint grow. &nbsp; 

This is a hands-on architecture role: you will define and evolve the AWS architecture, PostgreSQL data layers, and React-based frontends underpinning Label Traxx's integration ecosystem, resolve highly complex cross-cutting technical challenges spanning multiple systems, and drive the multi-year modernization strategy that extends Label Traxx's legacy 4D-based application through modern, AWS-native services. Deep, hands-on AWS expertise is required, since AWS underpins every integration in this ecosystem. 

You will partner with Amtech's Architecture Review Board and engineering leadership to set organization-wide standards for secure engineering, scalable architecture, CI/CD, automation, and AI-assisted development - and you will coach senior engineers across the Label Traxx and integrations teams to build lasting technical capability. 

We value engineers who embrace modern development practices, including collaborative Git workflows, CI/CD, Agile delivery, and responsible use of AI-assisted development tools to improve productivity and code quality. &nbsp; 

Key Responsibilities&nbsp; 

- Serve as the recognized technical authority for the Label Traxx ERP platform and its integration ecosystem, shaping engineering standards, architecture, and long-term technical direction. &nbsp; 
 - Own the AWS architecture underpinning all Label Traxx integrations - Cloud API, Batched, Siteline, Data Warehouse, and Supplier integrations - ensuring each is scalable, secure, and operationally mature on a shared cloud foundation. &nbsp; 
 - Drive the strategic roadmap for modernizing the legacy 4D-based Label Traxx platform, extending capability through AWS-native services across all integration points, and resolving highly complex cross-cutting technical challenges through expert judgment. &nbsp; 
 - Define and evolve PostgreSQL data architecture and modeling standards shared across Label Traxx's integrations, ensuring data integrity, performance, and consistency at scale. &nbsp; 
 - Guide architecture and technical direction for React-based frontends used by Label Traxx and its integration partners, ensuring consistency with backend and API design. &nbsp; 
 - Partner with the Architecture Review Board to define and evolve organization-wide standards for secure engineering, scalability, CI/CD, observability, and AI-assisted development practices. 
 - Improve engineering productivity, reliability, and delivery outcomes across the Label Traxx platform and its integration teams. &nbsp; 
 - Coach senior and staff-level engineers across Label Traxx and integration teams, influencing technical decisions and building organizational capability. &nbsp; 
 - Communicate technical direction, architecture decisions, and trade-offs to executive and cross-functional stakeholders (Product, Engineering, QA, Security, Operations). 
 - Evaluate AWS infrastructure and integration investments (compute, storage, networking, observability) needed to support Label Traxx's growth, reliability, and cost efficiency. &nbsp; 
 - Guide incident response and root-cause analysis for the most complex production issues spanning Label Traxx and its integrations. &nbsp; Skills & Qualifications&nbsp; 

- Bachelor's degree in Computer Science, Engineering, or related field (Master's a plus). &nbsp; 
 - 12+ years of software engineering experience, including significant time in technical leadership, architecture, or principal engineering roles. &nbsp; 
 - Deep, hands-on AWS expertise across multiple production services (e. g. , ECS/Fargate, API Gateway, DynamoDB, S3, Secrets Manager, CloudFormation/SAM) - able to define cloud architecture standards applied consistently across several integrations, not a single service. 
 - Proven experience architecting complex, integration-heavy enterprise platforms - designing and scaling multiple system-to-system integrations (APIs, batch processes, data warehousing, or supplier/EDI-style integrations). &nbsp; 
 - Strong PostgreSQL expertise, including data modeling, performance tuning, and schema design for high-transaction enterprise systems. &nbsp; 
 - Experience with React and modern frontend architecture; able to guide frontend/backend integration decisions. &nbsp; 
 - Strong background in C#/. NET (ASP. NET Core) and enterprise API design; proven experience modernizing legacy or monolithic systems into service-oriented or cloud-native architectures. 
 - Proven track record defining engineering standards, secure engineering practices, and CI/CD strategy across multiple teams. &nbsp; 
 - Demonstrated ability to mentor senior engineers and influence technical direction beyond a single team. &nbsp; 
 - Excellent communication skills; able to align technical and executive stakeholders on architecture, trade-offs, and risk. &nbsp; 
 - Experience guiding organization-wide adoption of AI-assisted development tools and practices is a plus. &nbsp; Why Join Amtech&nbsp; 

At Amtech, you will drive meaningful technical impact in a growing enterprise software organization while benefiting from Vista's world-class ecosystem. You'll collaborate with talented peers, leverage cross-portfolio learning programs, and help shape the future of Amtech's Label Traxx platform and its integration ecosystem. Build your career with Amtech - backed by the strength, scale, and innovation culture of Vista. &nbsp; 

