Job Summary&nbsp; 

We are seeking experienced UFT One Automation Engineers to support the migration of existing OPKEY automated tests to OpenText UFT One and modernize the automation framework for Oracle EBS and other enterprise applications. &nbsp; 

This role requires more than script conversion. Candidates should be able to analyze existing OPKEY assets, redesign and refactor tests where needed, build reusable UFT components, and establish a scalable and maintainable automation framework. &nbsp; 

Key Responsibilities&nbsp; 

- Analyze existing OPKEY automation assets and migrate/redesign them in UFT One. &nbsp; 
 - Design and implement scalable, reusable, and maintainable UFT automation frameworks. &nbsp; 
 - Automate Oracle EBS end-to-end business processes and regression scenarios. &nbsp; 
 - Develop reusable function libraries, actions, Object Repositories, test data utilities, logging, error handling, and reporting. &nbsp; 
 - Troubleshoot object identification, dynamic objects, synchronization, and execution issues. &nbsp; 
 - Convert existing manual and automated test cases into maintainable UFT solutions. &nbsp; 
 - Establish automation coding standards, framework standards, and best practices. &nbsp; 
 - Integrate automation assets with Git/Bitbucket and CI/CD tools. &nbsp; 
 - Support scheduled and unattended automated test execution. &nbsp; 
 - Collaborate with business SMEs, functional teams, developers, and QA teams to validate test coverage. &nbsp; 
 - Work collaboratively in an Agile/Scrum environment, participating in sprint planning, stand-ups, backlog refinement, reviews, and retrospectives. &nbsp; 
 - Provide technical documentation, knowledge transfer, and mentoring to QA team members. &nbsp; Required Skills&nbsp; 

- 8+ years of test automation experience with 4+ years of hands-on UFT One experience. &nbsp; 
 - Strong VBScript programming and debugging skills. &nbsp; 
 - Strong knowledge of Object Repository, Object Identification, Descriptive Programming, Actions, Checkpoints, Data Tables, Recovery Scenarios, and reusable components. &nbsp; 
 - Experience designing modular, reusable, data-driven, and/or keyword-driven automation frameworks. &nbsp; 
 - Experience with functional, regression, smoke, sanity, and end-to-end testing. &nbsp; 
 - Experience integrating Excel, CSV, XML, or other external test data sources. &nbsp; 
 - Experience with Git/Bitbucket and source-control practices. &nbsp; 
 - Strong troubleshooting, analytical, and problem-solving skills. &nbsp; Preferred Skills&nbsp; 

- Experience with OPKEY-to-UFT or similar automation platform migration/modernization projects. &nbsp; 
 - Hands-on experience automating Oracle EBS, including modules such as Order Management, AP, AR, GL, Purchasing, Inventory, and Fixed Assets. &nbsp; 
 - Experience with REST/SOAP API testing and JSON/XML validation. &nbsp; 
 - Experience with Jenkins, Bamboo, Azure DevOps, or other CI/CD platforms. &nbsp; 
 - Experience with Web, Angular, React, SAP, desktop, or terminal/mainframe applications. &nbsp; 
 - Ability to work independently and collaborate directly with business and technical stakeholders. &nbsp; Ideal Candidate&nbsp; 

We are looking for a hands-on UFT implementation and migration expert, not simply someone who develops UFT scripts. The candidate should have experience migrating and redesigning automation assets, building UFT frameworks, automating Oracle EBS business processes, resolving complex object-identification issues, and establishing automation standards for long-term maintainability and scalability. &nbsp; 

Salary: ₹16-24 LPA, negotiable for the right candidate. Candidates must be able to provide a minimum of 6 hours of overlap with US working hours.

Job brief: 

As a Customer Service and Sales Quality Assurance Manager your goal is to consistently ensure the highest quality of customer support across our Sales and customer support&nbsp; team by monitoring calls and providing actionable insights. The Quality Analyst gathers information to improve agent performance in the contact centre by upholding our internal quality standards and guidelines. The QA is responsible for identifying training needs and developing training programs for our agents. 

Providing an excellent customer experience is at the heart of what we do and your role will be a crucial part to ensure that this is upheld across all our customer-facing call centres. 

About the role

Do you love delighting customers? Join our growing team that will change the way Tyres are bought and sold in India!

As a Customer Service and Sales Quality Assurance Manager your goal will be to support our customers along their journey, as they inquire about Automotive products on our website, or need after sales support. You will receive all the necessary training you need to succeed in this role. We are looking for someone with a genuine passion for customer service, an energetic personality, and positive and proactive "can-do" attitude. You ideally have a minimum of 2 years experience in providing customer service via phone as well as excellent written email, chat and social media skills. Prior experience in customer service and sales in the Indian market is highly advantageous. This role will require weekend and after hours work based on a rotating roster. 

Responsibilities: 

● Maintain and develop internal support and call center quality standards; 

● Review a subset of support agents' conversations (calls, emails, chat, etc)

● Have Audits and super audits done along with weekly feedback sessions and reports

● Make sure the quality of calls is always above the industry standards and bring in new ideas of improving on the Quality of the team. Have calibration sessions with the team to ensure Quality assurance and understanding and improving the CSAT and NPS score. 

● Accompany evaluations with meaningful and constructive feedback; and explain feedback with agents in regular meetings; 

● Discuss Analyze all customer service and sales metrics and how the support team's performance affects those KPIs; 

● Create strategies to improve support KPIs; 

● Map the need for training and onboarding programs and initiate these projects; 

● Monitor customer service and sales performance on the agent and team level; 

● Create reports that reflect support performance and report support team's performance to higher-ups; 

● Contribute to the team culture in a positive manner. 

Requirements: 

● Experience in the customer service and sales space; 

● Proven track record of analytical skills; 

● Hands-on experience in quality assurance and extensive Training; 

● Quality analysis and audit experience; 

● Great people skills and ability to communicate constructive feedback; 

● Great organizational skills, knowledgeable in goal-setting practices; 

● Examples of data visualization abilities and understanding of support metrics; 

● Perception of basic business metrics and how support impacts those; 

● Problem-solving capabilities to create meaningful strategies to improve support quality. 

&nbsp; 

&nbsp;

For nearly 40 years, PDI has helped convenience retailers and petroleum wholesalers adapt to changes in the industry by leveraging the latest technologies. Simplifying the complexity in your world is our main focus. That's why we're delivering an integrated portfolio of global, cloud based solutions and services to meet our customers needs today and well into the future. From the back office to fuel logistics, and the latest wave of consumer demands and digital commerce, PDI solutions and services are designed to give you a competitive edge. Our deep domain knowledge is backed by our industry-specific software offerings and a people-first approach. Serving the entire supply chain means that we've had to solve a wide range of industry challenges and deliver measurable value. To address the increasingly dynamic convenience retail and petroleum wholesale industry, PDI leads the way with converged digital, cloud-optimized, secure, and scalable solutions including ERP, Loyalty, Fuel Pricing, Point-of-Sale and Logistics to create a broader industry ecosystem. The result is unparalleled insights, simplified operations, and higher profitability for your employees and business. We're dedicated to helping our more than 1, 500 customers in over 50 countries, providing solutions and services to over 200, 000 sites. 

Job Responsibilities: 

- Participate in design decisions for new and existing application development, proactively escalating issues and seeking assistance to overcome obstacles

- Prepare and provide project status and risk assessments to their manager with appropriate levels of detail to ensure that programs stay on schedule&nbsp; 

- Actively develop software solutions for PDI products&nbsp; 

- Perform testing to ensure systems meet documented user requirements&nbsp; 

- Use a disciplined approach in an Agile environment to assist in analysis and determination of preferred solutions to technical challenges&nbsp; 

- Troubleshoot, test, and validate software issues; resolve issues with due urgency and maintain thorough documentation of all software solutions&nbsp; 

- Compile test results to provide data for use in solving problems&nbsp; 

- Perform engineering level tests to find defects; troubleshoot and debug development and production issues, collaborating with QA Engineers to develop optimal product test plans&nbsp; 

- Work with Product Owner to clarify and estimate feature work&nbsp; 

- Work with QA Engineers to develop optimal product test plans and resolve new feature issues as QA finds bugs during release stabilization&nbsp; 

Qualifications: 

- 5-7 years' experience designing and developing new or maintaining existing software applications in a software product development environment

- Proficiency required in one or more of the following: . Net and C#, SQL, JavaScript or JavaScript Web Frameworks (e. g. React), ASP. Net MVC. &nbsp; 

- Proficiency with the Microsoft Visual Studio IDE and the use of Azure DevOps or Jira&nbsp; 

- Usage of AI development tools (ideally Claude) including agentic development methods&nbsp; 

- Experienced working with a full web stack or relational databases&nbsp; 

- Practical experience with SDLC and Agile methodologies&nbsp; 

- Highly motivated self-starter with a desire to help others and take action&nbsp; 

- Requires strong written and verbal communication skills with the ability to translate technical concepts into non-technical terms&nbsp; 

- Ability to independently work as a contributing member in a high-paced and focused team&nbsp; 

- Ability to multi-task and prioritize tasks with competing deadlines&nbsp; 

- Strong problem-solving and analytical skills with the ability to work under pressure

- Ability to socialize ideas and influence decisions without direct authority&nbsp; 

- Collaborative in nature with a strong desire to dig in and learn independently and as well as through asking questions&nbsp; 

- Considers 'best-practice' standards, as well as departmental policies and procedures&nbsp; 

- Computer science fundamentals: OOP, design patterns, data structures & algorithms&nbsp; 

Behavioral Competencies: 

- Cultivates Innovation

- Decision Quality

- Manages Complexity

- Drives Results

