Interplanetary Studios is building a patent-pending colonization architecture for the Moon, Mars and Venus, centered around a crewed multi-environment spaceplane, invented by Frederic Eger. 

Inventor Frederic Eger is looking for the head of engineering who turns the design into one controlled baseline, a department structure and a funded path from sub-scale demonstrators to the full vehicle. 

This is a Partner/Co-Founder role, not an employee job. &nbsp; 

It is a multi-decade commitment, but not a 9-to-5: 

keep other work if it never conflicts with ours, and we measure output, not hours. &nbsp; 

*The project must matter to you regardless of the money. *

What you'll do: 

1. Own the engineering baseline: requirements, data sheets, interface documents, change control; 

2. Own vehicle mass, power, thermal, volume and propellant budgets; 

3. Lead architecture trades and build the engineering departments; 

4. Drive verification and certification, from analysis to flight; 

5. Be our technical voice with investors, partners and regulators; 

What we're looking for: 

- Master's or higher in aerospace, mechanical or systems engineering; 
 - 12+ years in systems engineering, with a complete vehicle or safety-critical system taken through first flight, certification or field operation; 

Requirements: 

- MBSE (SysML), trade studies, failure analysis, safety cases; 
 - Founded or led a venture where your own money or reputation was at risk; 
 - Persistence: when the plan collapses, you come back with the next one; 

What you get: 

A founding-team seat with authority over the whole engineering organisation

Pre-funding: revenue share and/or ownership, agreed individually, plus a modest monthly expense allowance. No conventional salary until funding closes. 

